#' FSL FNIRT
#'
#' FSL FNIRT wrapper for non-linear registration
#'
#' @param in_file Character; file path. name of input image **Required.**
#' @param ref_file Character; file path. name of reference image **Required.**
#' @param affine_file Character; file path. name of file containing affine transform
#' @param apply_inmask Character or numeric vector. list of iterations to use input mask on (1 to use, 0 to skip)
#' @param apply_intensity_mapping Character or numeric vector. List of subsampling levels to apply intensity mapping for (0 to skip, 1 to apply)
#' @param apply_refmask Character or numeric vector. list of iterations to use reference mask on (1 to use, 0 to skip)
#' @param args Character. Additional parameters to the command
#' @param bias_regularization_lambda Numeric. Weight of regularisation for bias-field, default 10000
#' @param biasfield_resolution Character or numeric vector. Resolution (in mm) of bias-field modelling local intensities, default 50, 50, 50
#' @param config_file Character or numeric vector. Name of config file specifying command line arguments
#' @param derive_from_ref Logical. If true, ref image is used to calculate derivatives. Default false
#' @param field_file Character or numeric vector. name of output file with field or true
#' @param fieldcoeff_file Character or numeric vector. name of output file with field coefficients or true
#' @param hessian_precision Character; one of: "double", "float". Precision for representing Hessian, double or float. Default double
#' @param in_fwhm Character or numeric vector. FWHM (in mm) of gaussian smoothing kernel for input volume, default \[6, 4, 2, 2\]
#' @param in_intensitymap_file Character or numeric vector. name of file/files containing initial intensity mapping usually generated by previous fnirt run
#' @param inmask_file Character; file path. name of file with mask in input image space
#' @param inmask_val Numeric. Value to mask out in --in image. Default =0.0
#' @param intensity_mapping_model Character; one of: "none", "global_linear", "global_non_linear", "local_linear", "global_non_linear_with_bias", "local_non_linear". Model for intensity-mapping
#' @param intensity_mapping_order Integer. Order of poynomial for mapping intensities, default 5
#' @param inwarp_file Character; file path. name of file containing initial non-linear warps
#' @param jacobian_file Character or numeric vector. name of file for writing out the Jacobian of the field (for diagnostic or VBM purposes)
#' @param jacobian_range Character or numeric vector. Allowed range of Jacobian determinants, default 0.01, 100.0
#' @param log_file Character; file path. Name of log-file
#' @param max_nonlin_iter Character or numeric vector. Max # of non-linear iterations list, default \[5, 5, 5, 5\]
#' @param modulatedref_file Character or numeric vector. name of file for writing out intensity modulated --ref (for diagnostic purposes)
#' @param out_intensitymap_file Character or numeric vector. name of files for writing information pertaining to intensity mapping
#' @param ref_fwhm Character or numeric vector. FWHM (in mm) of gaussian smoothing kernel for ref volume, default \[4, 2, 0, 0\]
#' @param refmask_file Character; file path. name of file with mask in reference space
#' @param refmask_val Numeric. Value to mask out in --ref image. Default =0.0
#' @param regularization_lambda Character or numeric vector. Weight of regularisation, default depending on --ssqlambda and --regmod switches. See user documentation.
#' @param regularization_model Character; one of: "membrane_energy", "bending_energy". Model for regularisation of warp-field \[membrane_energy bending_energy\], default bending_energy
#' @param skip_implicit_in_masking Logical. skip implicit masking  based on value in --in image. Default = 0
#' @param skip_implicit_ref_masking Logical. skip implicit masking  based on value in --ref image. Default = 0
#' @param skip_inmask Logical. skip specified inmask if set, default false
#' @param skip_intensity_mapping Logical. Skip estimate intensity-mapping default false
#' @param skip_lambda_ssq Logical. If true, lambda is not weighted by current ssq, default false
#' @param skip_refmask Logical. Skip specified refmask if set, default false
#' @param spline_order Integer. Order of spline, 2->Qadratic spline, 3->Cubic spline. Default=3
#' @param subsampling_scheme Character or numeric vector. sub-sampling scheme, list, default \[4, 2, 1, 1\]
#' @param warp_resolution Character or numeric vector. (approximate) resolution (in mm) of warp basis in x-, y- and z-direction, default 10, 10, 10
